WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.035
-Thank you very much, Roots.
Hi, everybody.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.438
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.574
It is Monday, July 20th.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:09.743
There's a lot of news
to catch up on,

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.010
so let's get right into it.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.378
Guys, everybody is
talking about this.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.613
Yesterday, we got to see
President Trump's interview

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:17.583
with Chris Wallace on
"Fox News Sunday,"

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.954
and the reactions to
Trump's performance were mixed.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.488
Some experts called it a fiasco,

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:25.792
while others called it
a debacle.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.794
I'm not saying it was bad,
but by the end of it,

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:31.598
Kanye was calling for Trump
to get some help.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.733
Anyway, as the pandemic
continues to surge

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.202
across the country,
Wallace asked Trump about

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.738
a statement he previously made
about the virus

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:39.739
and whether
he still stands by it.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.174
Take a look.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.310
-I think we're going to be very
good with the coronavirus.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.112
I think that, at some point,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.147
that's going to sort of
just disappear.

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.783 line:0%
I'll be right eventually.
-[ Laughs ] I understand.

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.883
-I will be right eventually.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.452 line:0%
You know, I said,
it's going to disappear.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.187 line:0%
I'll say it again,
it's going to disappear,

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.688 line:0%
and I'll be right.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.391
-Yeah, he really believes this
is going to go away on its own.

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:01.260
Trump is like, "Everyone knows
the virus will disappear,

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.697
just like chicken pox
and herpes."

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.699
That's right -- Trump is just
going to keep ignoring it

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:12.238
until it disappears or, as he
calls it, "The Don Jr. Method."

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.506
Let me ask you a question.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.642
If your dermatologist said,
"That doesn't look good,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.009
but I'm sure it will
disappear eventually,"

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.379
would you keep going back?

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.214
During the interview,
Trump repeatedly knocked

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.182
Joe Biden as being unfit
for the job

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:26.119
and then challenged him to take
the same cognitive test

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.420
that he brags to have aced.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.688
Check it out.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:32.291 line:0%
-Let's take a test.
Let's take a test right now.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.527 line:0%
Let's go down, Joe and I.
We'll take a test.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.030 line:0%
Let him take the same test
that I took.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.631 line:0%
-Incidentally,
I took the test, too,

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:39.765 line:0%
when I heard that you passed it.

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:40.799 line:0%
-Yeah, how did you do?

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:42.234 line:0%
-Well, it's not
the hardest test.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.237 line:0%
There's a picture,
and it says, "What's that?"

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.238 line:0%
And it's an elephant.
-No, no.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:48.341
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:51.377
-Yeah, Trump was thinking,
"Damn it.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.745
I knew I should have written
down "elephant."

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:56.615
Elephant!
I wrote 'dinosaur.'"

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.918
I'm glad Trump knows how to
identify an elephant.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.853
If the country ever has an
elephant pandemic,

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.689
we'll be in great shape.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.257
Meanwhile, Don Jr. took the
test, but he just shot a hole

00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:09.828
in the picture of the elephant.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:11.865
Later in the interview,
Trump bragged about finding

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.367
all of the hidden objects in
a<i> Highlights</i> magazine.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.836
"I found the telescope,
the treasure chest.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.837
I found the diving helmet.
That was very hard to find.

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:21.006
That was in the seaweed."

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.508
Just to prove Trump
aced the test,

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:24.176
he spent the rest of
the interview

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:25.645
pointing at things
and naming them.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.947
"That's a chair. That's a tree.
This is a shirt.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.849
I can go all day."

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.252
Trump claims that doctors
were surprised how well he did.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.387
Mr. President, it's not good
when you have to take

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:40.726
a mental test and doctors are
surprised you did so well.

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:43.562
Well, we actually got ahold of
Trump's cognitive test,

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.764
and I'm not sure he did
as well as he claims.

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:47.099
I'll show you what I mean.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.902
For example, for the question,
"What is this shape?",

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:54.407
Trump wrote,
"A terrifying ramp."

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:58.911
Next up, for "List three words
that start with the letter 'J,'"

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:02.214
Trump wrote,
"Jobs, Jared, jenius."

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:05.351
Up next, for
"What is this color?",

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.287
Trump said, "Mirror color."

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:12.926
And for this question,
"What is this?",

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.994
Trump wrote, "My Twitter stick."

00:03:15.994 --> 00:03:18.898
And this was bizarre.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:22.034
For "Starting at 100,
count backwards from 7,"

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:26.372
Trump said, "7, 8, 9, 10,"
while he backed out of the room.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.742
And, finally, for
"What number is half of 50?",

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.610
Trump wrote,
"My approval rating."

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.978
Ooh.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:34.680
Later in the interview,
Wallace asked Trump

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.650
about the 2020 election
and what he would do if he lost.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.252
Listen to what Trump had to say.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:42.721 line:0%
-I think mail-in voting
is going to rig the election.

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.057 line:0%
-Are you suggesting that
you might not accept

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.390 line:0%
the results of the election?

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.292 line:0%
-You know, I have to see.
-Can you give a direct answer?

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:49.162 line:0%
You will accept the election?
-I have to see.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.730 line:0%
Look, you -- I have to see.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.231 line:0%
No, I'm not going to
just say "yes."

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.467
-Trump was like,
"I don't accept the results

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.469
of any elections at all.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:03:58.537
As far as I'm concerned,

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:01.774
Justin Guarini won
"American Idol."

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.242
The interview was so rough,
now everyone

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.944
who enters The White House
gets tested

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.779
to make sure
they're not Chris Wallace.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.014
"Just making sure."

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.149
These photos also of
Mark Zuckerberg

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.451
surfing in Hawaii.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.319
Did you see these yet?
Take a look at this.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.587
Him surfing.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.956
Can we zoom in
on his face at all?

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.659
Yeah. He's the Facebook C.E.O.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.662
He looks more like
the Snapchat logo.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:27.499
When reached for comment,
he said...

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:29.201
"Mime over matter"
is what I said.

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:33.973
I'm sorry. I forgot to...

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.175
Trump saw that and said,
"Oh, I know this one.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:39.578
It was on the test.
He's a swan."

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:41.680
After that, his wife changed
her relationship status

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.016
from married to
it's complicated.

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.651
Well, guys,
as the number of virus cases

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:46.985
continues to rise
here in the U.S.,

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:48.788
it sounds like
our neighbors to the north

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:51.190
are interested in extending
their travel ban.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.125
Listen to this
Canadian broadcast.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:57.463 line:0%
-IPSA's polling shows 93% of us
feel it's just too risky

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.732 line:0%
to travel to
the United States right now.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.234 line:0%
85% think the border
should stay closed

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.502 line:0%
until the end of the year.

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.671
-While the other 15%
of Canadians

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.840
were too nice to say anything.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.041
Man, Trump is going to be so mad

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:12.445
when they build their
border wall before we do.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.614
And, finally,
as the virus continues to spike,

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:17.550
you hope more people
will wear masks,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.718
practice social distancing,
and do their part

00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:21.253
to help stop the spread,

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:23.455
and then you hear
something like this.

00:05:23.455 --> 00:05:27.159
-A woman was told to leave
a Verizon Wireless store

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:29.462
after she refused
to wear a mask,

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.597
and rather than going quietly,

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:36.302
she decided to pee
all over the sales floor.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:39.538
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:42.208
-Employees were like, "Lady,
what do you think this is?

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:46.412
A P-Mobile?"

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.115
To be fair, Verizon did say
they offered

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.918
streaming anytime, anywhere.

